# Techno Sapiens Prompt Templates

Copy a template, replace `[placeholders]`, and send it to the assistant.

## Principles

- Reference rules with `@rule-name.mdc`. Include `@010-technosapiens-conventions.mdc` when needed.
- State the goal (new section, CPT, refactor).
- Include names, slugs, fields, design references, paths.
- Do not ask the AI to auto-write `.md` docs unless you name the file.

---

### 1. Creating a new section

```
@060-create-section.mdc @010-technosapiens-conventions.mdc @065-section-development.mdc

Create a new section called '[section-slug]'.

**Design Reference:** [Figma / screenshot / description]

**ACF Fields Needed:**
- [field_name_1] (type: [text|wysiwyg|image|repeater|select|true_false|...], required: [true|false])
- [field_name_2] (type: image)
- [field_name_3] (type: repeater)
  - [sub_field_1] (type: text)
```

Notes:

- `[section-slug]` is kebab-case with `section-` prefix, e.g. `section-hero`.
- Design reference is mandatory. The AI must ask if it is missing.
- Image fields should match `section-content` (return format array).
- Do not add margin fields; `section-settings.json` handles them.

---

### 2. Creating a custom post type & taxonomy

```
@080-post-types-conventions.mdc @010-technosapiens-conventions.mdc

Register a new custom post type named '[Post Type Name Singular]'.
- Post type slug: `[post-type-slug]`
- Labels: '[Singular]', '[Plural]'
- Supports: [title|editor|thumbnail|excerpt|...]
- Has archive: [true|false]
- Rewrite slug: `[rewrite-slug]`
- Menu icon: '[dashicon-slug]'

(Optional) Also register taxonomy '[Taxonomy Name Singular]'.
- Taxonomy slug: `[taxonomy-slug]`
- Hierarchical: [true|false]
- Associate with `[post-type-slug]`.
```

Slugs use kebab-case.

---

### 3. Refactoring to Techno Sapiens conventions

```
@010-technosapiens-conventions.mdc @015-code-formatting-consistency.mdc @[optional: 030/040/065]

Please refactor the following code in `[file-path.php]`.

**Goal:** Follow Techno Sapiens conventions for [naming|templating|styling|sections].

**Constraint:** Only change what is needed. Do not restyle existing working code. No inline styles or scripts.

**Existing Code:**
```php
// paste code
```
```
